      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To effectively illustrate this in your slides, you can show sample internal narrative notes contrasting the language used. For example, a manager might label a candidate speaking AAVE as having an \"understatement in tone\" or being \"laid back,\" while describing a peer with a standard accent as having a \"confident delivery\" and \"polished professional voice.\" Similarly, internal notes might reflect assumptions such as \"had to be clearer to understand\" for those with heavy accents versus \"integrated smoothly\" for those with neutral accents, despite their verbal performance being identical. Visually presenting these divergent internal monologs alongside identical hypothetical interview transcripts will powerfully highlight how bias dictates the narrative before any performance data is even analyzed.",
